# Claude Code. api.anthropic.com serves model traffic, the WebFetch domain check and feature flags.
allow https://api.anthropic.com/   read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE
allow https://api.anthropic.com/api/ws/speech_to_text/voice_stream upgrade=websocket  # /voice under --audio=mic
allow https://platform.claude.com/ read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # OAuth token exchange, refresh and revocation

# Measured with claude 2.1.319 and 2.1.323 on 2026-11-13 (doc/plan-tls-inspect-agents.md, "Measurement"):
# - Modes: an interactive session with tool calls, a subagent, a compaction, WebFetch and /voice under --audio=mic;
#   claude -p, as ko-review runs it. 2.1.323 repeated all but the subagent and WebFetch, and added /logout, a sign-in,
#   and a token refresh forced by moving the token's expiry into the past.
# - The path, refused and error lines are what MeasurementReport accepts (doc/plan-tls-inspect-agents.md, "The
#   measurement suite"). Each <...> stands for one segment or part of one; <org> is the organization's UUID.
#   path api.anthropic.com /v1/messages /v1/messages/count_tokens /v1/mcp_servers /v1/ultrareview/quota
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/oauth/profile /api/oauth/claude_cli/roles /api/oauth/account/settings
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/oauth/organizations/<org>/skills/list-skills
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/oauth/organizations/<org>/skills/<name>/download
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/oauth/organizations/<org>/plugins/list-plugins
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/oauth/organizations/<org>/marketplaces /api/organizations/<org>/model_selector/cc
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/claude_cli/bootstrap /api/claude_code_grove /api/claude_code_penguin_mode
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/eval/sdk-<key> /api/event_logging/v2/batch /api/artifacts/mcp
#   path api.anthropic.com /api/hello /api/web/domain_info /api/directory/plugins /api/directory/server-urls
#   path api.anthropic.com /mcp-registry/v0/servers /api/ws/speech_to_text/voice_stream
#   path platform.claude.com /v1/oauth/hello /v1/oauth/token /v1/oauth/token/revoke
#   path github.com /anthropics/claude-plugins-official.git/info/refs
#   path github.com /anthropics/claude-plugins-official.git/git-upload-pack
#   refused mcp-proxy.anthropic.com CONNECT
#   refused downloads.claude.ai CONNECT
#   refused http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com CONNECT
#   error api.anthropic.com client:
#   error api.anthropic.com relay: client: Broken pipe
# - The refusals are of hosts absent below. The errors: Claude Code reset three connections, two before the response
#   head reached it and one mid-upload; `relay: client: Broken pipe` as a client exited.
# - Requests without a credential: /api/hello, /api/web/domain_info, /api/directory/plugins,
#   /api/directory/server-urls and /mcp-registry/v0/servers; one /api/event_logging/v2/batch after /logout; every
#   request to platform.claude.com, whose codes and tokens travel in bodies.
# - The WebSocket at /api/ws/speech_to_text/voice_stream opens once per recording.
# - Every request body declared a Content-Length. Within each launch, every request that carried a credential showed
#   one index per token: the sign-in's and the refreshed token each as a new index.
# - A /v1/messages body names the previous response that it continues, and holds only the messages after it. The
#   client sends the whole transcript when the server's thread is gone or idle, so a request's size is not the
#   conversation's.
# - The interactive mode's git child fetches the official plugin marketplace from github.com, without a credential.

# These hosts of Claude Code's own list are absent (code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config):
# - claude.ai serves the sign-in pages, which open in the host's browser. No measured mode sent a request there.
# - mcp-proxy.anthropic.com serves the claude.ai connectors, which a claude.ai sign-in turns on by default.
#   - The host would open a write path to third-party services through an opaque tunnel. SECURITY.md prices the
#     same trade for Copilot's MCP.
#   - ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false silences the fetch.
# - The two Datadog intake hosts receive telemetry and error reports. Each attempt leaves a refusal in the log, or
#   none with CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC set.
# - downloads.claude.ai serves the auto-updater, its version checks and plugin executables.
# - claude.com serves the sign-in redirect page and pre-approved WebFetch documentation lookups.
# - *.claudeusercontent.com serves the Chrome extension's bridge, and artifact content, which the CLI reads when the
#   Artifact tool is available.
